<WovenDocs::Page
  @id="index"
  @title="WovenUI Ember kit"
  @subtitle="Glimmer components over the WovenUI SCSS component layer."
>
  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Overview" @id="overview">
    <p class="woven-doc__intro">
      The kit is one vocabulary in three packages: core tokens and
      utilities, an SCSS component layer, and the Ember components that
      drive it. Every component whitelists its variants, falls back to the
      default on a typo, spreads
      <code class="wu-code">...attributes</code>
      last on its root, and carries
      <code class="wu-code">data-test-wu-*</code>
      hooks on the root and on every interactive child.
    </p>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Features" @id="features">
    <ul class="wu-list">
      <li class="wu-list__item">Fifty-odd Glimmer components over one SCSS vocabulary, each documented with every variant live.</li>
      <li class="wu-list__item">One theme variable reskins the whole kit; per-component tokens retheme one instance.</li>
      <li class="wu-list__item">Right-to-left at both layers, verified with the Dir switch on every page.</li>
      <li class="wu-list__item">Four hosts and their services handle everything that floats.</li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Packages" @id="packages">
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="api" @rows={{this.packages}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Install" @id="install">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Styles"
      @note="Core first, then the kit. The kit entry forwards the token engine and loads every component sheet, utilities last."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.styles}}
    >
      <Woven::Text
        @size="sm"
        @muted={{true}}
        @text="Both sheets compile into one stylesheet; no runtime CSS is injected."
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Mount the hosts"
      @note="Four hosts render once in the application template, after the routed content and in this order. Tooltips, the anchored layer and dialogs share one z-index level and rely on paint order."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.hosts}}
    >
      <ul class="wu-list">
        <li class="wu-list__item">Modals and drawers render inline where they are used, so the layer paints above them.</li>
        <li class="wu-list__item">LayerHost before TooltipHost, so a tooltip on a menu item paints above the menu.</li>
        <li class="wu-list__item">Toasts sit one z-index level higher, above everything.</li>
      </ul>
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Theming" @id="theming">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @note="Modifiers reassign CSS variables; the base rule is the only consumer. Change --wu-brand and every m-primary surface follows. Retheme one instance by overriding its own --wu-{block}--{Property} token from outside."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.theme}}
    >
      <Woven::Text
        @size="sm"
        @muted={{true}}
        @text="The Theme switch in the topbar sets --wu-brand on the html element. Try it: every primary button, badge, toggle and focus ring on this site follows."
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Right-to-left" @id="rtl">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @note="The kit runs under a dir attribute on the html element with no per-use changes. The SCSS layer is RTL on its own (logical properties, mirrored keyframes); the components add reading-direction arrow keys, LTR pinning for numeric inputs and mirrored directional icons."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.rtl}}
    >
      <Woven::Text
        @size="sm"
        @muted={{true}}
        @text="The Dir switch in the topbar flips the whole site. Each component page lists its direction-specific behaviour under RTL."
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Pages" @id="pages">
    {{#each this.layout.navSections as |group|}}
      <h3 class="woven-subtitle">{{group.label}}</h3>
      <nav class="woven-toc" aria-label={{group.label}}>
        {{#each group.items as |entry|}}
          <LinkTo
            @route={{entry.route}}
            class="woven-toc__link"
            data-test-woven-toc={{entry.route}}
          >
            {{entry.label}}
          </LinkTo>
        {{/each}}
      </nav>
    {{/each}}
  </WovenDocs::Section>
</WovenDocs::Page>
